# Bossa: a bossa nova at ~128, written for Polly over C M7. Drums by hand (the Groove MIDI Dataset's bossa
# takes are improvised, the cross-stick sparse; a style needs the steady bossa clave).
# Main A: the cross-stick clave, soft hi-hat eighths, the bass on root and fifth with their pickups,
# a nylon guitar comping the syncopated pattern in 3rd-7th-9th voicings, soft strings.
# Main B: the ride, a shaker in sixteenths, a flute line, the strings up, the bass walking to the 3rd.
style Bossa
tempo 128

track d1 type=bypass chan=10 vol=96 rev=40
track d2 type=bypass chan=10 vol=96 rev=40   # shares channel 10 with d1: the same mixer
track pc type=bypass chan=10 vol=96 rev=40
track ba type=bass program=32 chan=2 lo=E1 hi=G3 hikey=F# vol=108 rev=24
track c1 type=chord1 program=24 chan=3 lo=E3 hi=G5 hikey=off vol=96 pan=46 rev=48
track c2 type=chord1 program=73 chan=4 lo=C5 hi=C7 hikey=F# vol=66 pan=82 rev=64
track c3 type=chord2 program=49 chan=5 lo=F3 hi=C5 vol=56 pan=64 rev=70 cho=20

[main a]
bars 2
beats 4
track d1
grid 1.1 s kick  6.....4.6.....4.|6.....4.6.....4.
grid 1.1 s rim   5.....5.....5...|....5.....5.....
grid 1.1 e chh   34343434|34343434
grid 1.2 h phh   44|44
track ba
